From b394ee721031788d8d60da4511ed65516a103030 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] avalanche: add quorum node-count and circulating-supply
 activation gates

Enforce organic Avalanche quorum node-count and staked circulating-supply
activation gates.

Original-Commit: 14192312769a7fda2627d1ec29dc91eef039bb6c
Original-Patch: v2/023
Split-Concern: whole

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Introduce native-only quorum node/supply parameters, original stake accounting and native fixture at their actual V2 owner, preserving the coherent shared quorum generation and upstream reward side effects. Omit duplicate adaptive/batch implementations, visitors, option definitions and independent atomic updater already supplied by shared owners. Original native gate behavior is retained; no new regression or timing in this application pass.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Absorb duplicate-only cleanup at first native quorum owner: keep one original quorum fixture (all unique assertions retained) and omit the unused query-timeout local. The later124 restoration/removal mailbox is redundant once earlier batches/visitors/options are retained once.
(cherry picked from commit 00863dfe20ef966dbad1b00da08bd5a4122a7596)

Canonical-Source-Commit: 00863dfe20ef966dbad1b00da08bd5a4122a7596
